    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4086" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as-sŏcĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ads-</span></b> ), āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to join to</i> or <i>unite with</i> a person or thing (post - Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornua summis Adsociant malis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. B. Gild. 482</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adsociati principali curae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
				1</span></i>
			, tit. 11.—<b>Poet.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mente virens Phoeboque Melampus Associat
					passus,</span>”
				<i>goes with</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 3, 454</span></i>
			 Queck.</div>
